---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TrustHero from "../components/TrustHero.astro";
import { siteUrl } from "../content";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Privacy Policy - Claude Model Insights",
  description:
    "Privacy policy for claudeopusmodels.com covering data collection, usage, GDPR, CCPA, and PIPEDA compliance.",
  url: `${siteUrl}/privacy-policy/`,
  datePublished: "2026-05-09",
  dateModified: "2026-05-09",
  inLanguage: "en-US",
  isPartOf: {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    "@id": `${siteUrl}/#website`,
  },
  about: {
    "@type": "Thing",
    name: "Privacy Policy",
    description:
      "Data protection and privacy practices for claudeopusmodels.com",
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Claude Model Insights"
  description="Privacy policy for claudeopusmodels.com. Learn how we collect, use, and protect your data. GDPR, CCPA, and PIPEDA compliant. Last updated May 2026."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  schema={schema}
>
  <TrustHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="How Claude Model Insights collects, uses, and protects your data. GDPR, CCPA, and PIPEDA compliant."
    accent="#7B7FA3"
    meta="Effective: May 9, 2026 · Last Updated: May 9, 2026"
  />

  <article class="trust-page">
    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      Claude Model Insights ("we," "us," "our") operates claudeopusmodels.com.
      We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal
      information. This Privacy Policy explains what data we collect, how we
      use it, and your rights regarding that data.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy applies to all visitors of claudeopusmodels.com, regardless
      of location. We comply with the EU General Data Protection Regulation
      (GDPR), California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), and Canada's Personal
      Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA).
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>2.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>
    <p>We collect information you voluntarily give us through:</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Contact form submissions:</strong> Your name, email address,
      and the contents of your message when you reach out through our contact
      page.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Newsletter signup:</strong> Your email address if you subscribe
      to our email updates. We don't collect any other personal data during
      signup.
    </p>
    <p>
      We don't require account creation to read our content. We don't
      process payments or collect billing information.
    </p>

    <h3>2.2 Information Collected Automatically</h3>
    <p>
      When you visit our site, certain data is collected automatically
      through cookies and similar technologies:
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Usage data:</strong> Pages you visit, time spent on each page,
      referring website, date and time of visit, and general browsing
      patterns.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Device data:</strong> Browser type and version, operating
      system, screen resolution, and device type (desktop, mobile, tablet).
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Network data:</strong> IP address, approximate geographic
      location (city/country level, not street address), and internet
      service provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      This data is collected through Google Analytics 4 (GA4) and, if
      enabled, Microsoft Clarity for heatmap and session replay analysis.
    </p>

    <h3>2.3 Information We Don't Collect</h3>
    <p>
      We don't collect social security numbers, financial information,
      health data, biometric data, or data from children under 16. We don't
      use facial recognition, voice recording, or keystroke logging
      technologies.
    </p>

    <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use collected information for these specific purposes:</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Responding to inquiries.</strong> When you contact us, we use
      your name and email to reply to your message.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Sending newsletters.</strong> If you subscribe, we send
      periodic email updates about new articles. Every email includes an
      unsubscribe link.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Understanding our audience.</strong> Analytics data helps us
      understand which articles are most useful, where our readers are
      located, and how we can improve the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Maintaining site security.</strong> We use technical data to
      identify and prevent security threats, spam, and abuse.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Complying with legal obligations.</strong> We may process data
      when required by applicable laws or regulations.
    </p>
    <p>
      We don't use your data for automated decision-making, profiling,
      targeted advertising, or selling to third parties.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
    <p>
      For visitors in the European Union and United Kingdom, we process
      personal data under these legal bases:
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Consent:</strong> For newsletter subscriptions and
      non-essential cookies. You can withdraw consent at any time.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Legitimate interest:</strong> For analytics (understanding our
      audience), site security, and improving our content. We've assessed
      that these interests don't override your privacy rights given the
      limited and non-sensitive nature of the data.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Legal obligation:</strong> When we're required to retain or
      disclose data by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How We Share Your Information</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>We don't sell your personal information.</strong> We never
      have, and we don't plan to.
    </p>
    <p>
      We share data with these categories of service providers, who process
      it on our behalf:
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Analytics providers:</strong> Google Analytics 4 (Google LLC,
      USA). Google's privacy policy:
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener"
        >policies.google.com/privacy</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Heatmap and session replay:</strong> Microsoft Clarity
      (Microsoft Corporation, USA), if enabled. Microsoft's privacy policy:
      <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com" rel="noopener"
        >privacy.microsoft.com</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Email service provider:</strong> For newsletter delivery, we
      use an email service that processes subscriber email addresses. The
      specific provider is identified in our newsletter emails.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Hosting provider:</strong> Our website hosting provider
      processes server logs that contain IP addresses and request data.
    </p>
    <p>
      All service providers are contractually obligated to protect your data
      and use it only for the purposes we specify.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may also disclose information when required by law, court order, or
      government request, or when necessary to protect our rights, safety,
      or property.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      We use cookies on this site. For detailed information about which
      cookies we use, their duration, and how to manage them, please see our
      <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Quick summary:</strong> We use essential cookies for site
      functionality and analytics cookies (GA4) to understand traffic
      patterns. We don't use advertising or marketing cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

    <h3>7.1 Rights for Everyone</h3>
    <p>Regardless of where you live, you can:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Unsubscribe from our newsletter at any time using the link in any email</li>
      <li>Contact us to ask what data we hold about you</li>
      <li>Request deletion of your personal data</li>
      <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>7.2 Additional Rights for EU/UK Residents (GDPR)</h3>
    <p>If you're in the European Union or United Kingdom, you also have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Restrict processing of your data</li>
      <li>Receive your data in a portable format (data portability)</li>
      <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interest</li>
      <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For UK residents, the supervisory authority is the Information
      Commissioner's Office (ICO) at
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>. For EU
      residents, contact your country's data protection authority.
    </p>

    <h3>7.3 Additional Rights for California Residents (CCPA)</h3>
    <p>If you're a California resident, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Know what personal information we collect, use, and disclose</li>
      <li>Request deletion of your personal information</li>
      <li>Opt out of the sale of personal information (we don't sell data, so this doesn't apply)</li>
      <li>Not be discriminated against for exercising your rights</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We don't sell personal information. We don't share personal
      information for cross-context behavioral advertising.
    </p>

    <h3>7.4 Additional Rights for Canadian Residents (PIPEDA)</h3>
    <p>If you're a Canadian resident, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access your personal information held by us</li>
      <li>Challenge the accuracy and completeness of your data</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent for data collection (subject to legal or contractual restrictions)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>7.5 How to Exercise Your Rights</h3>
    <p>
      Email us at
      <a href="mailto:contact@claudeopusmodels.com"
        >contact@claudeopusmodels.com</a
      > with your request. We'll respond within 30 days (45 days for CCPA
      requests if an extension is needed). We may need to verify your
      identity before processing certain requests.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We keep personal information only as long as necessary:</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Contact form messages:</strong> 2 years from the date of your
      inquiry, then deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Newsletter subscriber data:</strong> Until you unsubscribe,
      then deleted within 30 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Analytics data:</strong> Google Analytics retains data for 14
      months (our GA4 retention setting). After that period,
      individual-level data is automatically deleted by Google.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Server logs:</strong> Retained by our hosting provider for up
      to 90 days for security purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We protect your information using:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>SSL/TLS encryption for all data transmitted between your browser and our site</li>
      <li>Secure hosting infrastructure with regular security updates</li>
      <li>Access controls limiting who can view personal data</li>
      <li>Regular review of our data collection and processing practices</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No system is completely secure. While we take reasonable measures to
      protect your data, we can't guarantee absolute security of information
      transmitted over the internet.
    </p>

    <h2>10. International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Our site is operated from Pakistan. If you're visiting from outside
      Pakistan, your data may be transferred to and processed in countries
      that may not have data protection laws equivalent to your home country.
    </p>
    <p>
      For EU/UK visitors: We rely on Google's and Microsoft's Standard
      Contractual Clauses (SCCs) for data transferred to the United States
      through their analytics services.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our site isn't intended for children under 16. We don't knowingly
      collect personal information from anyone under 16. If you believe
      we've inadvertently collected data from a child, please contact us
      immediately at
      <a href="mailto:contact@claudeopusmodels.com"
        >contact@claudeopusmodels.com</a
      > and we'll delete it promptly.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>
      Our articles link to external websites (including Anthropic, GitHub,
      and various AI tools). We're not responsible for the privacy practices
      of these sites. We encourage you to review their privacy policies
      before providing them with personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>13. AI-Generated Content Disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      We use AI tools (including Claude) as part of our editorial process.
      AI tools don't have access to your personal data collected through
      this site. Our use of AI is limited to content creation and doesn't
      involve processing visitor personal information. See our
      <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. The "Last Updated"
      date at the top reflects the most recent revision. We encourage you
      to review this page occasionally. Significant changes will be
      communicated via a notice on our homepage.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy-related questions, concerns, or to exercise your rights:
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Email:</strong>
      <a href="mailto:contact@claudeopusmodels.com"
        >contact@claudeopusmodels.com</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Data Controller:</strong> Muhammad Younus, Claude Model
      Insights, Karachi, Pakistan
    </p>
    <p>
      We aim to resolve all privacy concerns directly. If we can't resolve
      your concern, you have the right to contact the relevant data
      protection authority in your jurisdiction.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
